# Can a stranger actually walk from the mine entrance to the first room?
#
#     build\RatnaBay.exe --yard --script Docs\scripts\walk.rbs
#
# smoke.rbs answers a different question. It turns on noclip and god and then
# `goto 0 -30`, teleporting through the wall into the room -- so it proves the
# room exists and is fightable, not that anyone can reach it. Its check was also
# `assert where has room`, which passes on the string "room 0", the answer you
# get standing at the entrance having gone nowhere.
#
# The one outside player this alpha has had spent 110 minutes in the corridor
# and never found the first room. Nothing in the gate could have caught that,
# because nothing in the gate walked.
#
# So: no noclip, no god, no goto, no move. `walk` holds W through the same
# controller and the same collision callback a player's keyboard does, so a wall
# stops it exactly as a wall should.

echo === down the free mine, as a new player ===

# The seed is pinned, and it has to be. A mine's chain leaves the entrance room
# on whichever side the walk chose, so on most seeds the way on is east or west
# and a script that can only hold W would walk into a wall and report a fault
# that is not there. 20789 leaves northward, and is the seed smoke.rbs already
# uses. What is being tested is the route, not the compass.
descend 1 20789
wait 2

# Entrance room, before going anywhere. Nothing is awake yet.
assert enemies has clear

echo === walk north, and keep walking ===

# The route is a straight line from the entrance: through the doorway, along the
# corridor, into room one. Roughly forty metres at 6 m/s, taken in stages so a
# failure says how far it got rather than only that it did not arrive.
look 0 0
walk 4
where

# The door out of the entrance room. It is shut, as every mine door is, and it
# opens on the first press because a mine door is not locked. It used to be
# emitted locked with Difficulty 0 -- openable, but reading "Locked  |  a key,
# or Security 0", which is a refusal with no verb in it. This is the press the
# one real player either never made or never believed would work.
assert use has Opened

walk 4
where
walk 4
where

echo === arrival ===

# The proof. Enemies only exist once RunRuntime.EnterRoom has run, which only
# happens when the player is physically inside the room volume. If the route is
# blocked, unlit past finding, or the trigger stops firing, there is nothing to
# list and this fails.
wait 2
assert enemies has Bandit
assert enemies not rising
shot captures/walk-room-one.png

echo === and it is a real fight, not an empty box ===

kill all
wait 0.5
assert enemies has clear

quit
